{"step_index":72,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-17T09:11:10Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-17T14:41:10+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-17T14:41:10+05:30\nCreated At: 2026-11-17T14:41:10+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-17T14:41:10+05:30\nShowing lines 1-87 of 87\n1: # Kezza Agent Rewards: macOS setup\n2: \n3: This is a separate platform from `Kezza_mobile-main`. It uses its own database, `kezza_rewards_db`; do not run these commands against `kezza_db`.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Install prerequisites\n6: \n7: - Python 3.11 or newer (the previous Python 3.9.6 installation is too old for this dependency set).\n8: - Node.js 20 or newer with npm (Node.js 20.9 or newer for the admin portal).\n9: - PostgreSQL 16 or newer.\n10: \n11: Homebrew is optional. Install it only if you want it to manage these tools. Install the current macOS Python and Node packages using Homebrew, then open a new Terminal window and verify with `python3 --version`, `node --version`, and `psql --version`.\n12: \n13: ## 2. Create an isolated PostgreSQL database\n14: \n15: Start PostgreSQL, then open its local administrative prompt. Create a dedicated login and database; use a new strong password in your own terminal:\n16: \n17: ```sql\n18: CREATE ROLE kezza_rewards_app LOGIN PASSWORD 'choose-a-strong-local-password';\n19: CREATE DATABASE kezza_rewards_db OWNER kezza_rewards_app;\n20: ```\n21: \n22: Verify the target before continuing:\n23: \n24: ```sh\n25: psql \"postgresql://kezza_rewards_app@127.0.0.1:5432/kezza_rewards_db\" -c \"SELECT current_database();\"\n26: ```\n27: \n28: The result must be `kezza_rewards_db`. If a database with this name already contains data, stop and take a backup/review before applying migrations.\n29: \n30: ## 3. Install backend packages and configure secrets\n31: \n32: Open Terminal in `kezza-agent-app/backend`:\n33: \n34: ```sh\n35: python3 -m venv .venv\n36: source .venv/bin/activate\n37: python -m pip install --upgrade pip\n38: python -m pip install -r requirements.txt\n39: cp .env.example .env\n40: ```\n41: \n42: Edit `backend/.env`. Set `DATABASE_URL` to the dedicated database and replace `JWT_SECRET_KEY` with a random value, for example:\n43: \n44: ```sh\n45: openssl rand -hex 32\n46: ```\n47: \n48: Keep `.env` private and do not add it to the ZIP, Git, or mobile app. Development OTP mode returns a code to the development client. Production SMS delivery requires a provider and secrets that Kezza has approved.\n49: \n50: ## 4. Apply the new schema and create the first administrator\n51: \n52: Run these commands from `backend/` with the virtual environment active:\n53: \n54: ```sh\n55: alembic upgrade head\n56: python -m scripts.bootstrap_super_admin\n57: ```\n58: \n59: The migration checks the connected database name and refuses to run unless it is `kezza_rewards_db`. The one-time bootstrap creates an OTP-only super-admin; it does not create a password or default account. Use an approved OTP provider before exposing the service outside local development.\n60: \n61: ## 5. Start the API\n62: \n63: ```sh\n64: uvicorn app.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n65: ```\n66: \n67: Check `http://127.0.0.1:8000/health`, `http://127.0.0.1:8000/health/db`, and `http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs`. The DB health check reports only `kezza_rewards_db` as healthy.\n68: \n69: ## 6. Configure and run the mobile app\n70: \n71: In a second Terminal window, open the project root and create a local `.env` from `.env.example`:\n72: \n73: ```sh\n74: cp .env.example .env\n75: npm install\n76: npm run start\n77: ```\n78: \n79: For iOS Simulator, set `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1`. For Expo Go on a phone, use the Mac's Wi-Fi IP address in place of `127.0.0.1`; the phone and Mac must be on the same network.\n80: \n81: ## 7. Run the admin portal\n82: \n83: Open `admin/`, copy `.env.example` to `.env.local`, set `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1`, then run `npm install` and `npm run dev`. Sign in using the super-admin mobile number and the backend OTP flow. The portal cannot create its own default credentials.\n84: \n85: ## Before a real rollout\n86: \n87: Kezza must approve the payout method, cycle calendar, threshold treatment, late approval/refund rules, and legal wording. Until then, a new policy remains a draft and reward cycle creation or payment approval is blocked where a decision is required. Production also needs an SMS/OTP provider, secure private object storage, backups, TLS, deployment secrets, and operational monitoring. The local uploads directory is only for development."}
